"Entropy photon-number inequality · QIQCOP Zoo (https://qiqc-op.com/problem/op_ba39e7a80122b256/)\nciteturn6view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://qiqc-op.com/problem/op_ba39e7a80122b256/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 119\nL0: cite0†QIQCOP QIQCZOO Quantum Information and Quantum ComputationOpen Problem Zoo cite1†Problems cite2†Tags cite3†About cite4†Contribute cite5†GitHub ↗†github.com L1: \nL2: Random cite6†Unsolved cite7†Solved L3: \nL4: cite0†Zoo ›cite1†Problems ›op_ba39e7a80122b256\nL5: \nL6: # Entropy photon-number inequality\nL7: \nL8: Unsolved ID `op_ba39e7a80122b256` Last edited 7 October 2026\nL9: \nL10: cite8†Edit†github.com Cite Share\nL11: \nL12: Field\nL13: \nL14: \nL15:   * cite9†Quantum Communication L16: \nL17: Topics\nL18: \nL19: \nL20:   * cite10†Bosonic channels L21:   * cite11†Matrix and entropy inequalities L22: ## Problem\nL23: \nL24: Does the entropy photon-number inequality hold for every pair of independent finite-energy bosonic inputs? Let \\(n\\geq1\\) and \\(0\\leq\\eta\\leq1\\). The input is \\(\\rho_A\\otimes\\rho_B\\), where each factor is an \\(n\\)-mode state with finite total mean photon number. Correlations among the modes within either factor are allowed. Mix corresponding input modes on beam splitters and retain the outputs\nL25: \nL26: \\begin{equation} c_j=\\sqrt\\eta\\,a_j+\\sqrt{1-\\eta}\\,b_j,\\qquad j=1,\\ldots,n. \\tag{1} \\end{equation}\nL27: Let \\(\\rho_C\\) be the joint state of the modes in Eq. cite12†(1) . Use natural logarithms, \\(S(\\rho)=-\\operatorname{Tr}\\rho\\ln\\rho\\), and \\(g(x)=(x+1)\\ln(x+1)-x\\ln x\\) for \\(x\\geq0\\), with \\(0\\ln0=0\\). The proposed inequality is\nL28: \nL29: \\begin{equation} g^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{S(\\rho_C)}n\\right) \\geq\\eta g^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{S(\\rho_A)}n\\right) +(1-\\eta)g^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{S(\\rho_B)}n\\right). \\tag{2} \\end{equation}\nL30: \nL31: Prove Eq. cite13†(2) in this full domain or provide a physical input pair that violates it.\nL32: ## Source\nL33: \nL34: The entropy photon-number conjecture is stated explicitly in De Palma, Mari, and Giovannetti, Sec. II.3, Eq. (34), with attribution there to the earlier Guha–Shapiro–Erkmen work cite14†[DMG14] .\nL35: ## Progress\nL36: \nL37: Reports do not certify correctness or automatically change the problem's status. cite15†Progress policy .\nL38: \nL39:   * The quantum entropy power inequality proves \\(e^{S(\\rho_C)/n}\\geq\\eta e^{S(\\rho_A)/n}+(1-\\eta)e^{S(\\rho_B)/n}\\). This is weaker than Eq. cite13†(2) . The same paper bounds the possible deficit in Eq. cite13†(2) by \\(1/2-1/e\\); see Eqs. (5) and (35) cite14†[DMG14] .\nL40:   * For \\(n=1\\) and a thermal second input with mean photon number \\(b\\geq0\\), Theorem 4, Eq. (24), proves \\(S(\\rho_C)\\geq g(\\eta g^{-1}(S(\\rho_A))+(1-\\eta)b)\\). Thermal first inputs attain equality. This permits arbitrary first inputs but does not permit an arbitrary nonthermal second input cite16†[DTG17] .\nL41:   * Reported progress: cite17†Issue #103†github.com (withdrawn).\nL42:   * OpenAI reports a proof of Eq. cite13†(2) for two independent finite-energy bosonic inputs and any finite number of modes (Theorem 1.1, p. 2) cite18†[OAI26] . Arbitrary entanglement among modes within either input is allowed. Product thermal inputs attain equality, including when the two input entropies differ.\nL43: ## Comment\nL44: \nL45: The preprint cite18†[OAI26] reports a proof in the full finite-energy domain stated above; the catalog retains the Unsolved designation while documenting this report. Independence of the two input systems is essential. Taking one input to be vacuum yields the finite-energy case of the catalog’s multimode constrained pure-loss output-entropy question.\nL46: ## References\nL47: \nL48: cite14†[DMG14] L49:     G. De Palma, A. Mari, and V. Giovannetti, “A Generalization of the Entropy Power Inequality to Bosonic Quantum Systems,” Nature Photonics 8, 958–964 (2014).cite19†DOI†doi.org cite20†arXiv†arxiv.org L50: \nL51: cite16†[DTG17] L52:     G. De Palma, D. Trevisan, and V. Giovannetti, “Gaussian States Minimize the Output Entropy of One-Mode Quantum Gaussian Channels,” Physical Review Letters 118, 160503 (2017).cite21†DOI†doi.org cite22†arXiv†arxiv.org L53: cite18†[OAI26] L54:     OpenAI, “The entropy photon-number inequality,” OpenAI Math Release preprint, 24 September 2026. cite23†manuscript (release version)†github.com .cite23†link†github.com L55: ## Related problems\nL56: \nL57: ## Page edit log\nL58: \nL59:   * Record created 10 September 2026\nL60:   * Last edited 7 October 2026\nL61:   * Revisions 3\nL62: \nL63: cite24†View the full history on GitHub†github.com L64: \nL65: ## Your contribution is welcome!\nL66: \nL67: cite25†Submit a progress report with an archival manuscript or paper link, or cite26†link an earlier GitHub report . For a correction, cite27†describe the correction on GitHub†github.com or cite8†edit this record†github.com and open a pull request. See the cite28†contribution guide .\nL68: ## Cite this page\nL69: \nL70: “Entropy photon-number inequality,” Quantum Information and Quantum Computation Open Problem Zoo (QIQCOP Zoo), ID op_ba39e7a80122b256, accessed 2026-10-08.\nL71: \nL72: Use the Cite button above for BibTeX and the permanent link.\nL73: \nL74: ## Cite this problem\nL75: \nL76: [Button: ×]\nL77: \nL78: Please also cite the primary sources listed under References. Cite this page for the statement, status, and stable identifier.\nL79: ### BibTeX\nL80: \nL81:     @incollection{qiqcop_op_ba39e7a80122b256,\nL82:       title = {Entropy photon-number inequality},\nL83:       booktitle = {Quantum Information and Quantum Computation Open Problem Zoo (QIQCOP Zoo)},\nL84:       year = {2026},\nL85:       howpublished = {\\url{https://qiqc-op.com/problem/op_ba39e7a80122b25